B.a8L=new A.c5("What is this?","Calculates the height loss expected after a single engine failure during AW139 OEI hover operations, following the three-graph method from the Flight Manual Performance Charts.",null)
B.a8i=new A.c5("1 \u2014 Gross Weight","Enter the aircraft all-up weight in kg (4 400 \u2013 6 800 kg) or lb (9 700 \u2013 14 991 lb). Toggle the kg/lb button to switch units \u2014 values are converted automatically. The correct chart (\u2264 6 400 kg or > 6 400 kg) is selected automatically.",null)
B.a8G=new A.c5("2 \u2014 Pressure Altitude",'Enter the pressure altitude of the hover site in feet.\nUse "Calculate from MSL & QNH" to convert from a QNH setting if needed.',null)
B.a8c=new A.c5("3 \u2014 OAT","Enter the outside air temperature in \xb0C.",null)
B.a8e=new A.c5("4 \u2014 Headwind","Enter the headwind component in knots. Use 0 for calm conditions.",null)
B.a8p=new A.c5("5 \u2014 Result","The estimated height loss in feet is shown when the inputs are within the chart boundaries. The red line traces the three-graph path: Graph 1 (PA / OAT) \u2192 Graph 2 (AUW) \u2192 Graph 3 (Headwind) \u2192 Height loss.",null)
B.a8j=new A.c5("Limits","If the combination of inputs falls outside the chart envelope a warning is displayed and no result is computed. Adjust one or more inputs to return within limits.",null)
B.a8b=new A.c5("Chart","Tap the chart to open it full-screen with pan and zoom. Labels on the red dots show the OAT / altitude (Graph 1), weight (Graph 2), headwind (Graph 3) and the final height loss.",null)
